tk-linux-kapi: generic Linux kernel-API shims (LinuxKPI layer)
================================================================

Moved from `crates/ax/tk-intel-gt/src/linux/` (Linux 7.2.3 interface and
implementation references are retained in module comments). The source
identifiers recorded below apply to the functions translated from those files;
they do not reclassify TheKernel-authored adapters or type-only records.

  assert.rs, bitmap.rs, bits.rs, config.rs (generic part), dma.rs,
  drm_mm.rs, firmware.rs, gem_memory.rs (generic records), heap.rs, idr.rs,
  iomapping.rs, kernel_core.rs, kernel_services.rs, list.rs, locks.rs,
  memory.rs, mm.rs, mm_native.rs, mmu_notifier.rs, mutex.rs, print.rs
  (printk and drm_printf basics), rbtree.rs, rcu.rs, rcu_work.rs,
  scatterlist.rs, seq_file.rs, shmem.rs, signal.rs, srcu.rs, tasklet.rs,
  timer.rs, vm.rs, wait.rs, workqueue.rs, ww_mutex.rs, xarray.rs,
  fields.rs (generic records), primitives.rs (generic helpers).

New translations in this crate:

  completion.rs   kernel/sched/completion.c, include/linux/completion.h
                  (GPL-2.0-only; waiters poll `done`, see module note)
  seq_buf.rs      lib/seq_buf.c, include/linux/seq_buf.h (subset;
                  GPL-2.0-only)
  iopoll.rs       include/linux/iopoll.h (GPL-2.0-only;
                  poll_timeout_us and the read/readx families)
  i2c.rs          drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c subset (adapter, msgs,
                  quirks, add/del, transfer, bus lock) with
                  include/uapi/linux/i2c.h flags (GPL-2.0-or-later source;
                  UAPI header is GPL-2.0-or-later WITH Linux-syscall-note)
  i2c_algo_bit.rs drivers/i2c/algos/i2c-algo-bit.c and
                  include/linux/i2c-algo-bit.h (full; GPL-2.0+ / GPL-2.0-or-later)

