DRM V2 / synchronization additions and source status (checked against the
local Linux 7.2.3 tree):

- `dma_fence.rs`, `dma_fence_array.rs`, `dma_fence_chain.rs`, and
  `dma_fence_unwrap.rs` follow `drivers/dma-buf/{dma-fence.c,
  dma-fence-array.c,dma-fence-chain.c,dma-fence-unwrap.c}` and their
  `include/linux/dma-fence*.h` headers. The C files and relevant headers carry
  `GPL-2.0-only`. Original copyright lines: dma-fence.c © 2012 Canonical Ltd
  and © 2012 Texas Instruments; dma-fence-array.c © 2016 Collabora Ltd and
  © 2016 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; dma-fence-chain.c © 2018 Advanced Micro
  Devices, Inc.; dma-fence-unwrap.c © 2022 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.
- `sync_file.rs` follows `drivers/dma-buf/sync_file.c` and
  `include/linux/sync_file.h` (`GPL-2.0-only`; header copyright © 2012 Google).
  The C source also carries © 2012 Google.
- `dma_resv.rs` follows `drivers/dma-buf/dma-resv.c` (`MIT`) and
  `include/linux/dma-resv.h` (no SPDX line; it contains the VMware dual-license
  permission text and the Canonical/Linaro/TI attribution). Its Rust file
  currently carries an MIT SPDX comment.
- `irq_work.rs` follows the `init_irq_work()` / `IRQ_WORK_INIT()` interface in
  `kernel/irq_work.c` and `include/linux/irq_work.h` (`GPL-2.0-only`); source
  copyright © 2010 Red Hat, Inc., Peter Zijlstra.

The GPL source identifiers above are reflected by GPL SPDX comments on the
corresponding Rust translations. `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt` and
`LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt` are verbatim copies of Linux 7.2.3
`LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0`, including its identifier metadata and complete
version 2 license text. `Cargo.toml` records the package mix as
`MIT AND GPL-2.0-only AND GPL-2.0-or-later`.

GPU-driver specific code (i915 and intel GT records, GuC/GuC-log and
GMBUS-specific helpers, the i915 wait-var active-reference wait, and the
i915 GEM/list macros) stays in tk-intel-gt and is not part of this crate.
